@startuml
!include style/ail.puml
title G5 · Borrow timing: region end versus earlier invalidation
hide footbox
$caller(caller, "Caller\nUses the returned view")
$callee(view, "view\nBorrows its input during the call")
$owner(store, "Store\nOwner of the viewed bytes")
== Synthetic immutable store ==
caller --> view : Entry: lend store; valid($store, call)
activate view
note over view : Input validity lasts through completion.
view --> caller : Completion: deliver borrow(owner($store))
deactivate view
note over caller, store
  Caller may use the returned view while Store lives.
  invalidated_by([]): no earlier operation invalidates it.
end note
store ->x caller : Store destruction: returned view becomes invalid
== Constructed mutable variant, separate from the fixture ==
caller --> view : Entry: lend store; valid($store, call)
activate view
view --> caller : Completion: deliver borrow(owner($store))
deactivate view
note over caller, store : Caller may use this view until an invalidator or owner destruction.
store ->x caller : replace entry: old view becomes invalid
note over caller, store
  Store remains alive; the old view is already unusable.
  Later Store destruction cannot restore that view.
end note
legend bottom
  Time runs downward within each separate case; spacing is not duration.
  Actor = caller; rectangle = callee; circle on base = owner; bar = active view call.
  Dashed arrow = borrowed access; marked end = invalidation, not caller destruction.
  Returned validity outlives the input call region. Non-normative: C1, C5.
  Other clauses and the mutable variant's full operation contracts are omitted.
endlegend
@enduml
